# Kconfig for WiFi Ultra Low Power module

menuconfig ENABLE_WIFI_ULTRA_LOWPOWER
    bool "Enable WiFi Ultra Low Power"
    default n
    depends on ENABLE_WIFI
    help
        Enable the WiFi Ultra Low Power (ULP) module.
        This provides a reference-counting based power manager (lpmgr)
        that automatically adjusts CPU sleep cycles and WiFi DTIM
        values based on active system operations.
        
        When enabled, applications can use lpmgr_register/lpmgr_unregister
        to control power states, while the SDK automatically manages
        transitions during network operations.
